@ivan-hc please adhere to the following format for modules

```
# modules name
# function definations

function func_a() {
# Do one thing and do it well
}

function func_b() {
# Do one thing and do it well
}

function initial_vars_if_needed() {
# Do one thing and do it well
}

function _mududeName_main() {
# core logic that will also be defined in APP-MANAGER
}


_mududeName_main


exit;
                    if [check if the script is running from shell or sourced by APP-Manager]  [for future ref]
                        # run _mududeName_main() if not being source by APP-Manager  [for future ref]


```

- `-s` : only AM, modules and check for updates in the installation scripts of the apps installed (maybe one of them has been improved, by replacing the symlink with a script, see kdenlive and avidemux...);
- `-u` : updates all the installed apps and also calls `-s`, it is an all-in-one option.

In both cases, AM and all the modules are always updated to the latest version.

About AM numbes, this is my personal scheme (and thinking):
- x = structural changes of APP-MANAGER (see the last 6, with modularity and 5, where AM and AppMan were one thing);
- x.x = new feauture (options);
- x.x.x = improved new feature;
- x-x or x.x-x or x.x.x-x = not major/minor releases, but bug fixes or a way to notice people that something is changed.

